{"availability":"available","full":"927tanmay/react-ai-voice-avatar","name":"react-ai-voice-avatar","description":"Open-source alternative to real-time avatar APIs like HeyGen Interactive Avatar and Tavus. A talking, lip-synced 3D avatar that runs on your user's GPU, driven by your own LLM. No video stream, no per-minute billing. Or voice mode alone, ChatGPT-style, as a headless React hook. 📦 npm: react-ai-voice-avatar","category":"Developer tools","language":"TypeScript","stars":18,"forks":4,"created":"2026-08-03T20:59:08Z","updated":"2026-10-07T11:00:47Z","license":"MIT","branch":"main","homepage":"https://react-ai-voice-avatar.vercel.app/","topics":["ai-avatar","conversational-ai","headless","heygen-alternative","hindi","kokoro","lipsync","onnx","r3f","react","react-hook","speech-to-speech","threejs","tts","virtual-assistant","voice-ai","voice-assistant","voice-mode","webgpu","whisper"],"demo":"https://react-ai-voice-avatar.vercel.app/","color":"#63362a","ink":"#f8c7a8","lastCheckedAt":"2026-10-08T20:08:01.685Z","lastAttemptAt":"2026-10-08T20:08:01.685Z","lastAvailableAt":"2026-10-08T20:08:01.685Z","lastDemoCheckedAt":"2026-10-04T08:17:48.541Z","discoveredVia":[],"metrics":[{"at":"2026-10-03T10:45:07.783Z","stars":14,"forks":1},{"at":"2026-10-04T08:17:48.541Z","stars":15,"forks":1},{"at":"2026-10-06T16:30:00.793Z","stars":17,"forks":2},{"at":"2026-10-08T20:08:01.685Z","stars":18,"forks":4}],"technologies":["React","Three.js"],"overview":{"kind":"readme","version":1,"paragraphs":["The open-source alternative to real-time avatar APIs, as a React component.","You bring the model. Point it at OpenAI, Anthropic, your own fine-tune or your existing chat endpoint, and keep your keys on your own backend. The package owns the parts that are tedious to build and easy to get wrong: microphone capture, knowing when someone has finished speaking, interrupting the avatar mid-sentence when they talk over it, streaming speech synthesis, and driving 52 ARKit facial blendshapes at 60 FPS so the mouth matches the words.","It can also run with no backend at all. Speech recognition, generation and voice all have in-browser implementations, which makes for a convincing demo and a genuinely offline kiosk. Most production apps will use their own model and keep only speech and lip-sync on the device."],"features":[],"sourceUrl":"https://github.com/927tanmay/react-ai-voice-avatar/blob/main/README.md","fingerprint":"4519d441282c5a08506bb67cb140b53260d9e8a9ed75027ea30d285317a1c651","extractedAt":"2026-10-07T02:55:56.290Z"},"overviewCheckedAt":"2026-10-07T02:55:56.290Z","projectInsights":{"version":1,"whatItDoes":{"text":"The open-source alternative to real-time avatar APIs, as a React component.","sourceUrl":"https://github.com/927tanmay/react-ai-voice-avatar/blob/main/README.md"},"audience":[],"requirements":[],"fingerprint":"4519d441282c5a08506bb67cb140b53260d9e8a9ed75027ea30d285317a1c651","sourceUrl":"https://github.com/927tanmay/react-ai-voice-avatar/blob/main/README.md","checkedAt":"2026-10-07T02:55:56.291Z"},"overviewRepoUpdated":"2026-10-06T13:47:32Z","readmeSnapshot":{"version":1,"status":"saved","sourceUrl":"https://github.com/927tanmay/react-ai-voice-avatar/blob/main/README.md","checkedAt":"2026-10-07T02:55:56.292Z","hash":"4519d441282c5a08506bb67cb140b53260d9e8a9ed75027ea30d285317a1c651","originalBytes":59981,"storedBytes":59981,"truncated":false,"searchTerms":["voice","avatar","model","text","local","speech","string","when","const","browser","one","void","models","which","own","what","onsubmit","react","kokoro","return","undefined","webgpu","api","only","tsx","conversation","while","without","engine","microphone","true","user","demo","headless","language","nothing","where","custom","download","react-ai-voice-avatar","still","about","app","first","hindi","import","live","reply","turns","hearing","hook","memory","same","audio","boolean","default","each","keep","once","page","rather","speaking","whisper","any","backend","before","react-three"